From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fill the gaps Microsoft 365 hits on startup

Measured against Word from a real Click-to-Run install, each one found by
running it and reading what it said, in the order it said them:

twinapi.appcore: implement IAnalyticsInfoStatics2 and answer DeviceForm.
  Click-to-Run's service activates Windows.System.Profile.AnalyticsInfo and
  QueryInterfaces for IAnalyticsInfoStatics2; Wine had the class but not that
  interface, so it got E_NOINTERFACE, which C++/WinRT turned into a thrown
  exception that killed the service. The IID and the vtable order are read from
  Windows' own Windows.System.winmd (scripts/winmd-query.py). The one attribute
  ever asked for is n:TriggeredFlightIds, which a machine on no flight ring
  does not have -- so an empty map is the right answer, not a placeholder, and
  the operation is complete the moment it is created.

kernel32/kernelbase: OOBEComplete, FindPackagesByPackageFamily,
  SetFileShortNameW. All three were absent or commented-out stubs. A delay
  import that cannot bind raises rather than returning an error, so absence is
  worse than a failing implementation.

combase/ole32: CoRegisterActivationFilter. Wine has no activation filtering, so
  the filter is accepted and never consulted -- the same outcome as a machine
  where nothing is filtered.

sppc: SLLoadApplicationPolicies, SLGetApplicationPolicy, SLFreeApplicationPolicies.
  Refusing to open the policy set and opening an empty one are different to the
  caller: the first reads as a broken licensing stack, the second as a machine
  with no policies. Office takes the second and carries on.

ntdll: name the failing delay import. The MSVC helper raises
  VcppException(ERROR_MOD_NOT_FOUND/ERROR_PROC_NOT_FOUND) with a DelayLoadInfo
  and Wine said nothing about it, so a process dying on one left no trace of
  which import it was. This is what identified CoRegisterActivationFilter.
(cherry picked from commit c2ba7da21dfe2679e595f25607a5bf6285410b48)

